Architecture plan for Issue #152: Add a POST update route for admin post edits

Current architecture:
- Next.js App Router frontend/admin UI lives under app/ and components/.
- Admin post forms in app/admin/posts/_components/post-editor-form.tsx submit multipart forms directly to Rust API endpoints.
- Rust Axum backend lives under rust-backend/src, with route registration centralized in rust-backend/src/main.rs.
- Admin post CRUD handlers live in rust-backend/src/posts/admin.rs; update_admin_post already handles multipart updates for an existing post.
- Existing API consumers can update posts through PUT /api/admin/posts/:id.

Issue implementation plan:
- Minimal backend-only route wiring change in rust-backend/src/main.rs.
- Add POST /api/admin/posts/:id/update to the admin post route set and route it to posts::admin::update_admin_post.
- Preserve existing PUT /api/admin/posts/:id behavior for API consumers.
- No new shared types, database migrations, frontend changes, or dependencies are required.

Design decisions:
- Keep all admin mutation auth/validation/storage cleanup logic in the existing update_admin_post handler to avoid divergence between PUT and form POST paths.
- Add or update tests only if needed to prove the route is registered; otherwise existing handler-level coverage remains sufficient.
- The change is independent and has no dependency on other issues.
